node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# THE MEASUREMENT TAPES ARE NOT IN THE TREE. Dry dock phase C untracked all 705 of them for
# repository hygiene — a lighter tree and faster clones — and for nothing else. They are in this
# repository's public commit history and untracking cannot un-publish them, so the move claims no
# confidentiality and buys none. They are published as the public `slot-zero-data.tar.gz` asset on
# the `data-2026-08-02` release, and `config/data-root.mjs` owns where a run reads them from.
# README.md → "Where the data lives".
#
# Both paths are anchored (`/data/…`) so this ignores the two tapes and nothing else that
# happens to be named the same further down the tree, and they are named ONE PER LINE rather
# than as `/data/` so a THIRD dataset is not silently ignored the day someone adds one.
/data/population-tape-2026-07-29/
/data/graduated-life-tape-2026-08-02/

# There are no credentials in this repo and there must never be. These lines exist so an
# accidental one is not committed, not because anything here reads them.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
